<p>President Donald Trump said a new oil refinery is planned for the Port of Brownsville in Texas. He described it as the first new major U.S. refinery in about 50 years and credited India’s Reliance Industries as a partner and investor. Trump promoted the project on Truth Social, framing it as part of his push to raise U.S. energy production and exports, and as a boost for national security and economic growth. Several basic details are still unclear—or look disputed across the coverage. Trump called it a “$300 billion” deal, but multiple reports said he did not explain the figure, and it may refer to something broader than the refinery itself. Dawn noted that plans previously described by Element Fuels for a Brownsville refinery carried a much smaller estimate of $3–$4 billion, highlighting the gap between earlier descriptions and the headline number Trump cited. Reliance had not publicly responded to Trump’s announcement in the reporting cited here.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zDFdBcV4bHrfj_AG4K6-HeC0iqqfVX5yZVMEkuS04ZkL68OcB2RFAOJxP_5qnmJd39fEYWeU7JMcyesqK-5jxdbktuLPKoa299YsAENl0ymb' alt='A Reuters file photo shows an advertisement for Reliance Industries at a construction site in Mumbai, India (2016).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Project operator: Trump said America First Refining would build the facility; coverage describes it as an Element Fuels project.</li><li>Shale focus: Element Fuels’ materials say the refinery is designed to run on 100% American shale oil, tying the concept to U.S. light-oil supply.</li><li>Investment claim: America First Refining says it secured a “9-figure investment” at a “10-figure valuation” and signed a 20-year agreement to buy, process, and distribute shale oil.</li><li>Energy context: RT connected the announcement to heightened Middle East tensions that briefly lifted oil prices, a reminder of how geopolitics can sharpen interest in domestic refining capacity.</li></ul><blockquote>America is returning to REAL ENERGY DOMINANCE! Today I am proud to announce that America First Refining is opening the FIRST new U.S. Oil Refinery in 50 YEARS - Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He framed the announcement as a “historic” deal and “the biggest in US history,” and thanked Reliance for a “tremendous Investment,” but did not spell out Reliance’s specific commitment. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980847/trump-touts-us-oil-refinery-deal-with-indias-energy-giant-reliance-industries'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>The Hindu: It said it was not immediately clear whether Trump’s figure referred to the refinery itself or to a broader framework involving India. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-announces-oil-refinery-in-texas-us-thanks-partner-india-reliance-investment/article70728556.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>America First Refining: The company says the U.S. has ample light shale oil but not enough refining capacity built for it, and it pitches the project as a way to create jobs and strengthen supply chains. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/india/634460-indian-refiner-to-invest-in/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-announces-oil-refinery-in-texas-us-thanks-partner-india-reliance-investment/article70728556.ece'>Trump announces opening of oil refinery in Texas, thanks India’s Reliance for ‘tremendous’ investment</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980847/trump-touts-us-oil-refinery-deal-with-indias-energy-giant-reliance-industries'>Trump touts US oil refinery deal with India’s energy giant Reliance Industries</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-announces-first-us-oil-refinery-in-50-years-thanks-reliance-13988256.html'>Trump announces first US oil refinery in 50 years, thanks Reliance</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/president-donald-trump-announces-new-us-oil-refinery-with-investment-from-indias-reliance-company-11198101#publisher=newsstand'>Trump Announces New US Oil Refinery With Investment From Reliance</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/india/634460-indian-refiner-to-invest-in/'>Indian refiner to invest in $300 billion Texas facility – Trump</a> - rt.com</li></ul>